\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related}

\paragraph{Model Collapse Theory.}
\citet{shumailov2024_nature} demonstrate that recursive training on model outputs erodes distributional tails; \citet{dohmatob2024_tale_of_tails} formalize tail narrowing vs.\ cutting, with extensions to strong collapse \cite{dohmatob2025_strong_collapse} and the regression case \cite{dohmatob2024_demystified}; the MAD framework \cite{alemohammad2024_mad} quantifies precision--recall tradeoffs in self-consuming models.
Mitigation includes data retention \cite{gerstgrasser2024_accumulate}, detection-based filtering \cite{drayson2025_detection_prevents_collapse}, and curated pipelines \cite{falahati2026_curated}; recent work further identifies non-monotonic dynamics \cite{bakshi2026_collapse_improvement}, fixed-point convergence \cite{marchi2024_heat_death}, contamination bounds \cite{wang2026_contamination}, knowledge collapse \cite{knowledge_collapse2025}, spectral signatures \cite{sigma2026_spectral}, and self-improving loops \cite{synthetic_eggs2026}.
These works characterize degradation but assume depth is known; we address the inverse problem.

\paragraph{AI Text Detection.}
The detection literature \cite{wu2025_detection_survey} spans statistical methods---DetectGPT \cite{mitchell2023_detectgpt}, Fast-DetectGPT \cite{fast_detectgpt2024}, Binoculars \cite{binoculars2024}, DivEye \cite{diveye2026}, GLTR \cite{gehrmann2019_gltr}---model-based classifiers \cite{verma2024_ghostbuster,yang2024_dnagpt,wang2024_m4_semeval}, and watermarking \cite{kirchenbauer2023_watermark}.
Fundamental limits exist: paraphrasing reduces detection to near chance \cite{sadasivan2023_paraphrase}, detection degrades under distribution shift \cite{pudasaini2026_detection_fails}, and a generator barrier bounds performance \cite{pu2026_generator_barrier}.
All perform binary classification; our approach outputs ordinal depth labels.

\paragraph{Adjacent Tasks.}
Adjacent work addresses related but distinct problems: EditLens \cite{editlens2026} estimates editing extent, \citet{uchendu2020_attribution} classify which model generated text, LOKI \cite{loki2025} benchmarks multimodal detection, and \citet{mohamed2025_broken_telephone} measure forward degradation in iterative generation; none estimates recursive depth.
CORAL \cite{coral2020} and CLOC \cite{cloc2025} provide ordinal classification frameworks we adopt as baselines (\S\ref{sec:generalization}).

\paragraph{Decoding Strategy Effects.}
Decoding strategies shape text statistics in ways relevant to depth: nucleus sampling maintains diversity \cite{holtzman2020_nucleus}, strategy effects are model-dependent \cite{garces_arias2025_decoding_decoded,wiher2022_decoding}, parameters affect evaluation non-trivially \cite{finlayson2024_closing}, and Mirostat \cite{basu2021_mirostat} directly regulates perplexity.
Our atlas (\S\ref{sec:atlas}) reveals these strategies induce qualitatively different degradation trajectories under recursive generation.
