Llama-3.1-8B matches smaller models at $\mathrm{EDD}{=}4$ with monotonic AUC decay; Qwen2.5-7B achieves $\mathrm{EDD}_{T{=}0.70} > 5$ via a non-monotonic (U-shaped) trajectory where AUC recovers after a d2v3 minimum (consecutive AUC profiles in Table~\ref{tab:cross_scale_auc_full}, Appendix~\ref{app:cross_scale_auc}).
Per-step signal strength decreases at larger scale (mean consecutive AUC 0.78 vs.\ 0.85 at 1--1.5B), and the divergent trajectories suggest instruction tuning may alter degradation dynamics, though further architectures are needed.
Cross-model recursive chains (84.75\%) and cross-domain transfer (arXiv 74.1\%) further confirm signal universality (Appendix~\ref{app:cross_boundary}).
